  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Multi-Sectoral Humanitarian Assistance to Drought-Affected Displaced Communities in Marsabit and Isiolo in Kenya</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Compounded by climate change, communities in the dry region of Kenya are driven to migrate in search of essential assistance and resources. The vulnerable population displaced by prolonged droughts face significant challenges in accessing basic needs such as food, water, hygiene, health, education, and infrastructure. 
 
In this project, IOM is providing multi-purpose cash assistance to internally displaced persons and host communities in Marsabit and Isiolo Counties. The cash assistance is informed by deployment of IOM&#x2019;s Displacement Tracking Matrix (DTM) to generate up-to-date data on climate-induced displacement and the needs of the internally displaced persons (IDPs).</narrative>
  </description>
